# MASTER DEVELOPMENT PROMPT
# FloodGuard – AI-Powered, Community-Driven Flood Risk Intelligence and Emergency Safe-Route Management System

## 1. Project Overview

Build a complete, functional, responsive web application named **FloodGuard**.

FloodGuard is an AI-powered, community-driven flood risk intelligence and emergency safe-route management platform designed to help citizens, emergency responders, and government authorities make informed decisions before, during, and after floods.

The system should combine:
- Real-world geographical and weather datasets.
- Flood-risk assessment.
- AI-assisted analysis.
- Graph-based route optimization.
- Real-time community reporting and route feedback.
- Emergency resource management.
- Multilingual voice interaction.
- Offline emergency support.
- Citizen and expert dashboards.

**Default geographical scope:** Pune and Pimpri-Chinchwad, Maharashtra, India.

The architecture must be modular so that other cities and geographical regions can be added later.

Do not create only a static UI or a collection of dummy dashboards. Build a working end-to-end application with functional backend APIs, data processing, database integration, risk calculation, routing algorithms, and realistic demonstrations.

